WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.127 --> 00:00:02.545
<i>Previously on</i> Fightland...

2
00:00:02.712 --> 00:00:03.855
<i>Heavyweight Champ of the world...</i>

3
00:00:03.879 --> 00:00:05.297
<i>My not so little brother.</i>

4
00:00:05.464 --> 00:00:06.733
I couldn't have gotten
here without you. you know.

5
00:00:06.757 --> 00:00:07.757
Get his hands!

6
00:00:10.428 --> 00:00:11.428
Calvin...

7
00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:13.179
Why?!

8
00:00:13.264 --> 00:00:14.932
<i>Freeze! Do not move!</i>

9
00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:16.535
<i>You were fucking
Kingsley Marshall's wife.</i>

10
00:00:16.559 --> 00:00:18.352
Boxing is a criminal enterprise.

11
00:00:18.519 --> 00:00:20.312
<i>Always has been. and always will be.</i>

12
00:00:20.479 --> 00:00:21.939
<i>Yeah. I heard about Kingsley.</i>

13
00:00:22.106 --> 00:00:23.899
<i>No one's seen
or heard from him in months.</i>

14
00:00:24.066 --> 00:00:25.906
<i>Maduka Kilroy's just
been released from prison.</i>

15
00:00:26.068 --> 00:00:28.404
<i>is it true he's coming to
work for Marshall Promotions?</i>

16
00:00:28.571 --> 00:00:30.531
Yeah. that's right.

17
00:00:35.244 --> 00:00:36.328
And the operation?

18
00:00:36.454 --> 00:00:37.872
<i>We frame the Albanians.</i>

19
00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:40.249
<i>and a very bloody internal war starts.</i>

20
00:00:40.416 --> 00:00:42.710
One that Kingsley will be forced
out of his hole to stop.

21
00:00:42.877 --> 00:00:44.003
and I'll take it from there.

22
00:00:44.128 --> 00:00:45.588
It was you who hit the warehouse.

23
00:00:47.089 --> 00:00:48.257
What's goin' on here Duke?

24
00:00:48.424 --> 00:00:49.943
Son of a bitch has a recording device.

25
00:00:49.967 --> 00:00:51.567
- You and him working together?
- No! No!

26
00:00:51.635 --> 00:00:52.845
He's not goin' anywhere.

27
00:00:53.012 --> 00:00:54.406
'till I figure out what's goin' on here.

28
00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:56.182
If not? He's dead.

29
00:00:56.474 --> 00:00:58.100
And so are you. Duke.

30
00:01:03.564 --> 00:01:05.065
Let's all just relax...

31
00:01:11.155 --> 00:01:12.758
What're you sayin'. mate?!
What's he fuckin' sayin'?!

32
00:01:12.782 --> 00:01:14.426
- Duke. what's he say in?!
- Jay. shut the fuck up!

33
00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:16.530
Just shut up. Lazaro. listen
to me. put the gun down.

34
00:01:16.577 --> 00:01:18.496
- Just listen to me.
- Why are you here?

35
00:01:21.165 --> 00:01:22.416
Why are you here. Jay?

36
00:01:22.583 --> 00:01:23.727
Gazzer said that
you was actin' odd. right?

37
00:01:23.751 --> 00:01:25.294
Said you were comin' and goin'.

38
00:01:25.461 --> 00:01:27.022
Yeah. he gave me this address
that you wrote down...

39
00:01:27.046 --> 00:01:28.648
All right. all right. all right. all right.

40
00:01:28.672 --> 00:01:30.049
<i>On a magazine. so I followed it.</i>

41
00:01:30.174 --> 00:01:31.842
- How do I know we can trust him?
- <i>We?!</i>

42
00:01:32.009 --> 00:01:33.487
Me and Duke have been best
mates since we were ten. wanker!

43
00:01:33.511 --> 00:01:34.821
Who the fuck are you
to question my loyalty?!

44
00:01:34.845 --> 00:01:36.325
I'm the one holding the gun. pendejo!

45
00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:38.110
Lazaro! Look at me.
Look at me. look at me.

46
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:46.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

47
00:01:47.233 --> 00:01:49.276
I wouldn't risk that for anyone.

48
00:01:50.444 --> 00:01:51.487
All right?

49
00:01:53.864 --> 00:01:55.115
You have my word.

50
00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:04.583
Your word ain't worth the risk-

51
00:02:09.171 --> 00:02:10.714
Then do us both.

52
00:02:11.757 --> 00:02:13.077
And then you can explain to Amado

53
00:02:13.175 --> 00:02:15.177
why his entire plan died with us.

54
00:02:19.014 --> 00:02:20.414
Otherwise. put the fuckin' gun down

55
00:02:20.516 --> 00:02:22.142
and let's get back to work.

56
00:02:26.021 --> 00:02:27.021
All right.

57
00:02:27.439 --> 00:02:29.024
<i>If they're not together...</i>

58
00:02:30.609 --> 00:02:33.153
who the hell is that?
And what's he doing here?

59
00:02:33.612 --> 00:02:35.197
Zeek and CeCe's cousin...

60
00:02:35.364 --> 00:02:36.364
Simeon.

61
00:02:40.828 --> 00:02:42.872
He must have followed me from the gym.

62
00:02:56.886 --> 00:02:58.178
The hell?

63
00:02:59.722 --> 00:03:01.473
If he's workin' with the cops.

64
00:03:02.516 --> 00:03:04.560
we need to figure out what they know.

65
00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:07.938
Let me try somethin'...

66
00:03:12.693 --> 00:03:14.296
All right. we need to find
out more about Simeon.

67
00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:16.238
Keep his phone. see what comes up.

68
00:03:16.947 --> 00:03:18.282
Van's probably been made.

69
00:03:18.449 --> 00:03:20.784
I'll dispose of it and our <i>compañero</i> here.

70
00:03:21.619 --> 00:03:22.762
But you need to get to the dockyard

71
00:03:22.786 --> 00:03:24.246
and on to the next step.

72
00:03:25.372 --> 00:03:27.041
No. Duke. what does he mean.
"next step?"

73
00:03:27.166 --> 00:03:29.376
Where the fuck
did all this gear come from?

74
00:03:30.169 --> 00:03:31.337
Hey?

75
00:03:32.129 --> 00:03:33.129
Duke?!

76
00:03:33.297 --> 00:03:35.007
This belonged to Kingsley.

77
00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:37.593
Belonged?

78
00:03:38.344 --> 00:03:40.697
Wait. what-you-you stole it?
Are you-are you fuckin' mad?

79
00:03:40.721 --> 00:03:42.616
Look. if Kingsley finds out.
he's gonna come after ya.

80
00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.308
Yeah. that's exactly what I want.

81
00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:47.114
I'll get into it all later. but right now.

82
00:03:47.144 --> 00:03:48.744
there's somethin' I got to take care of.

83
00:03:48.854 --> 00:03:49.956
All right. well I'm gonna have
to come with you. aren't I?

84
00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.398
You ain't goin' anywhere.

85
00:03:51.565 --> 00:03:52.709
What. you expect me to sit
here and twiddle my thumbs?

86
00:03:52.733 --> 00:03:53.943
No chance.

87
00:03:54.109 --> 00:03:55.462
Besides. 'Livin La Vida Wanker'
over there

88
00:03:55.486 --> 00:03:56.796
just said your van has been made.

89
00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:57.881
So. unless you wanna book an Uber?

90
00:03:57.905 --> 00:03:59.114
I'm your best bet.

91
00:04:01.075 --> 00:04:02.576
<i>So. where the fuck are we going?</i>

92
00:04:02.743 --> 00:04:04.596
Hear the dockyard they ship
from ain't far from here.

93
00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:05.913
A guy named Nadim runs it.

94
00:04:06.038 --> 00:04:07.081
Albanian geezer. is it?

95
00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:08.749
- Yeah.
- Yeah. name rings a bell.

96
00:04:08.916 --> 00:04:10.727
I did some collection work
for his crazy ass son. Lorik.

97
00:04:10.751 --> 00:04:13.128
Well. they run a fleet of stolen
luxury cars every month

98
00:04:13.295 --> 00:04:15.714
inside shipping containers
headed all across Europe.

99
00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:18.467
We're gonna plant the
stolen drugs in one of 'em.

100
00:04:19.134 --> 00:04:20.260
Here. left here.

101
00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:23.680
<i>Fuckin' hell. mate.</i>

102
00:04:23.806 --> 00:04:24.682
Plantin' drugs?

103
00:04:24.807 --> 00:04:26.007
Killin' Simeon. what the fuck?

104
00:04:26.141 --> 00:04:27.726
Why the fuck are you doin' this. Duke?

105
00:04:29.019 --> 00:04:30.771
The attack in Vegas...

106
00:04:34.316 --> 00:04:35.442
it was a hit.

107
00:04:36.443 --> 00:04:38.237
And Kingsley ordered it.

108
00:04:40.197 --> 00:04:42.199
Well. now you're fuckin'
havin' a laugh. ain't ya?

109
00:04:42.324 --> 00:04:43.659
Kingsley loved you and Calvin.

110
00:04:43.826 --> 00:04:45.828
He treated you like sons.
why would he do that?

111
00:04:47.621 --> 00:04:49.289
'Cause he loved his business more.

112
00:04:50.249 --> 00:04:53.669
Yeah. he found out
that I was gonna leave him...

113
00:04:53.836 --> 00:04:55.170
sign with Colman.

114
00:04:56.255 --> 00:04:57.673
Slow down.

115
00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:59.466
Damn. I had no idea.

116
00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:03.679
Right. okay. so-so what is this?

117
00:05:03.846 --> 00:05:05.973
This is-this is revenge or something?

118
00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:10.894
Kingsley took everythin'
from me that night.

119
00:05:14.356 --> 00:05:15.441
My brother...

120
00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:19.445
my championship...

121
00:05:22.072 --> 00:05:23.157
my life.

122
00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.578
And now I'm gonna take
everythin' away from him.

123
00:05:28.871 --> 00:05:30.039
Brick by brick.

124
00:05:32.082 --> 00:05:33.082
And then?

125
00:05:35.044 --> 00:05:36.128
I'll kill him.

126
00:06:48.951 --> 00:06:50.077
Fuck's sake Jay.

127
00:06:50.244 --> 00:06:51.596
You can't go up here. it's no entry.

128
00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:52.871
No. no. no. no. it's fine.

129
00:06:53.038 --> 00:06:54.307
I'm gonna go up here
and turn left at the end.

130
00:06:54.331 --> 00:06:56.625
- It'll be quicker.
- Fuck.

131
00:06:56.792 --> 00:06:57.792
<i>Fuck. Jay!</i>

132
00:07:00.796 --> 00:07:01.880
Shit!

133
00:07:02.005 --> 00:07:03.285
All right. pull over. pull over.

134
00:07:07.803 --> 00:07:09.555
<i>All right. cover the stash. quick!</i>

135
00:07:10.514 --> 00:07:12.558
Easy. easy. easy. calm down. calm down.

136
00:07:12.724 --> 00:07:14.601
- Just calm down.
- Okay. Okay.

137
00:07:20.023 --> 00:07:21.275
<i>He's coming.</i>

138
00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:29.634
Ask me to hand you your license.

139
00:07:29.658 --> 00:07:30.658
What?

140
00:07:31.243 --> 00:07:32.327
Okay.

141
00:07:32.452 --> 00:07:33.972
You pulled an illegal move back there.

142
00:07:34.079 --> 00:07:35.399
Do you have your license. please?

143
00:07:35.873 --> 00:07:37.708
Yeah. yeah. of course officer...

144
00:07:37.875 --> 00:07:39.835
you mind handing me my
license. will you Duke?

145
00:07:40.002 --> 00:07:41.002
Yeah.

146
00:07:42.004 --> 00:07:43.338
Shit.

147
00:07:44.381 --> 00:07:45.381
You're Duke Kilroy.

148
00:07:45.465 --> 00:07:46.258
One and only.

149
00:07:46.425 --> 00:07:47.593
Yeah.

150
00:07:47.759 --> 00:07:49.320
What'd you go.
about cruiser weight. yeah?

151
00:07:49.344 --> 00:07:50.846
No?

152
00:07:51.013 --> 00:07:53.283
Yeah man. fighters can always
spot another fighter. innit?

153
00:07:53.307 --> 00:07:54.933
When I was comin' up. I used to...

154
00:07:55.058 --> 00:07:58.228
I used to spar with the officers
in training for the Lafone Cup.

155
00:07:58.353 --> 00:07:59.353
- Right.
- Yeah. yeah.

156
00:07:59.479 --> 00:08:00.647
Yeah. yeah. yeah. yeah. yeah.

157
00:08:00.814 --> 00:08:01.916
You's are some tough brothers. man.

158
00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:03.400
Well...

159
00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:07.088
What the hell are you's doin'
out at this time of night?

160
00:08:07.112 --> 00:08:07.946
We're actually headin'
off to a training session.

161
00:08:08.113 --> 00:08:09.323
ain't we?

162
00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:10.508
He's thinkin' of givin' it another run.

163
00:08:10.532 --> 00:08:11.533
Yep. just-Shh.

164
00:08:11.658 --> 00:08:13.018
Keep that between us though. yeah?

165
00:08:15.287 --> 00:08:16.705
How 'bout a selfie officer?

166
00:08:17.623 --> 00:08:19.475
- Yeah. go on then.
- Yeah. go on. I'll take it.

167
00:08:19.499 --> 00:08:20.709
All right. man.

168
00:08:21.835 --> 00:08:23.045
- Here we go.
- How you doing?

169
00:08:23.212 --> 00:08:25.047
- That's it.
- Yeah. yeah. that's-

170
00:08:25.214 --> 00:08:26.006
All right...

171
00:08:26.131 --> 00:08:28.258
Okay... yeah. lovely.

172
00:08:28.425 --> 00:08:30.594
- Here you go mate.
- Listen-thanks. Thanks.

173
00:08:30.761 --> 00:08:32.361
Yeah bruv. so your secrets safe with me.

174
00:08:32.429 --> 00:08:34.598
But get that brake light fixed.

175
00:08:34.765 --> 00:08:35.765
Okay?

176
00:08:36.141 --> 00:08:38.018
- You's have a good night.
- All right. man.

177
00:08:43.732 --> 00:08:45.234
Fuck. All right. let-we gotta go.

178
00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:46.520
- Let's go. Let's go.
- Yeah.

179
00:08:47.778 --> 00:08:50.018
<i>We need to hurry up man or we're
gonna miss the shipment.</i>

180
00:10:22.914 --> 00:10:24.124
<i>Shit.</i>

181
00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:27.960
Fuck!

182
00:10:34.968 --> 00:10:37.346
Lazaro. we didn't make it...

183
00:10:37.471 --> 00:10:38.889
no. we took a wrong turn.

184
00:10:39.806 --> 00:10:41.391
Yeah. I know we're runnin' out of time.

185
00:10:43.101 --> 00:10:44.853
We'll have to find another Albanian spot

186
00:10:45.020 --> 00:10:46.271
to plant the stash.

187
00:10:48.148 --> 00:10:50.484
Look. bruv we're gonna fix this all right...

188
00:10:50.942 --> 00:10:52.319
You've done enough.

189
00:10:52.486 --> 00:10:53.629
All right. it was a mistake
bringing you along.

190
00:10:53.653 --> 00:10:55.238
Just take me back to the spot.

191
00:11:06.249 --> 00:11:07.626
<i>So. Zeek Marshall.</i>

192
00:11:07.793 --> 00:11:09.544
<i>tell our viewers about your big plans.</i>

193
00:11:09.669 --> 00:11:11.838
In twenty-four hours' time.
we're gonna to turn this

194
00:11:12.005 --> 00:11:15.425
hallowed arena into the
epicenter of UK boxing again.

195
00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:18.053
<i>From the music.
to the lighting. to the food.</i>

196
00:11:18.220 --> 00:11:20.722
A Marshall's Promotions fight
isn't just a fight.

197
00:11:21.056 --> 00:11:22.391
it's an extravaganza.

198
00:11:22.557 --> 00:11:26.186
This is your first event
leading Marshall Promotions.

199
00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:29.272
What does it mean to you to be
bringing your first fight night

200
00:11:29.398 --> 00:11:30.941
to the magnificent York Hall?

201
00:11:31.066 --> 00:11:33.193
A place where legends are made.

202
00:11:33.652 --> 00:11:34.820
It means everything to me.

203
00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:37.864
This is where young Zeek first
fell in love with boxing.

204
00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:41.535
Come there with my dad.
watching fights together...

205
00:11:42.369 --> 00:11:43.870
it's a special part of my youth.

206
00:11:44.037 --> 00:11:46.790
Well Kingsley. he's shown
great faith in you. hasn't he?

207
00:11:46.957 --> 00:11:48.757
He's put you in charge
of the family business.

208
00:11:48.834 --> 00:11:51.086
but the question we all want to know.

209
00:11:51.545 --> 00:11:52.545
where is he?

210
00:11:52.587 --> 00:11:54.047
Is he coming back?

211
00:11:55.966 --> 00:11:57.402
Mind if we take a five-minute break?

212
00:11:57.426 --> 00:11:59.136
- I'm a bit parched.
- Yeah. yeah. sure.

213
00:11:59.302 --> 00:12:01.142
Do you think we can get
Cebella on camera next?

214
00:12:01.221 --> 00:12:03.098
Good luck with that one.

215
00:12:03.265 --> 00:12:05.142
You're lookin' well. you know. Anna.

216
00:12:08.979 --> 00:12:11.815
Has Simeon put the word out
on the street about our stash?

217
00:12:12.190 --> 00:12:14.651
He hasn't shown up this morning.

218
00:12:16.069 --> 00:12:17.749
He ain't been picking up his phone either.

219
00:12:18.697 --> 00:12:20.697
Fuckin' knows how important
this is for me as well.

220
00:12:21.116 --> 00:12:22.742
We do have another issue.

221
00:12:23.326 --> 00:12:25.829
The robbery exposed holes
in our operation.

222
00:12:26.913 --> 00:12:28.641
Our friends in Africa
reached out with concerns

223
00:12:28.665 --> 00:12:30.500
about sending us another shipment.

224
00:12:31.168 --> 00:12:33.712
They won't until those holes are plugged.

225
00:12:34.921 --> 00:12:37.549
- No shipments means no money.
- Mmhmm.

226
00:12:38.675 --> 00:12:40.677
Money we need to run
the boxing business.

227
00:12:40.844 --> 00:12:42.596
And the casino expansion.

228
00:12:45.474 --> 00:12:47.434
Dad couldn't have picked

229
00:12:47.601 --> 00:12:49.811
a better time for his little vanishing act.

230
00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:53.640
It's been six months and
we still haven't heard a word.

231
00:12:55.275 --> 00:12:56.860
You don't think he's-

232
00:12:58.737 --> 00:12:59.905
Dad isn't dead.

233
00:13:01.156 --> 00:13:02.574
You don't know that.

234
00:13:03.825 --> 00:13:07.454
What I know is in business.
if you've killed the King.

235
00:13:07.621 --> 00:13:09.247
you'd want the world to know about it.

236
00:13:09.748 --> 00:13:12.083
No value wearing
a crown in the shadows.

237
00:13:12.667 --> 00:13:14.044
Maybe.

238
00:13:14.753 --> 00:13:16.273
But what if they don't care about that

239
00:13:16.379 --> 00:13:18.840
because this ain't about
business to them. it's personal?

240
00:14:09.558 --> 00:14:10.892
Been looking all morning.

241
00:14:11.059 --> 00:14:12.745
if there's another place
to plant the Marshall stash

242
00:14:12.769 --> 00:14:15.105
on the Albanians and Nadim.
I don't see it yet.

243
00:14:15.564 --> 00:14:17.857
<i>We need to hit the streets.
scour for another spot.</i>

244
00:14:17.983 --> 00:14:19.234
I can't.

245
00:14:19.401 --> 00:14:21.321
It's my first day working
at Marshall Promotions.

246
00:14:21.736 --> 00:14:24.281
Your friend Jay.
if he's gonna be joining us.

247
00:14:24.447 --> 00:14:26.241
<i>know he's your responsibility.</i>

248
00:14:26.408 --> 00:14:27.728
You ain't got to worry about him.

249
00:14:28.368 --> 00:14:30.662
Anyway. I gotta get to work.
and while I'm there.

250
00:14:30.829 --> 00:14:32.390
I'm going to find out
what I can about Simeon.

251
00:14:32.414 --> 00:14:35.000
Okay. I want to know the
minute you find anything.

252
00:14:41.339 --> 00:14:44.759
1-2.1-2.1-2. That's it.

253
00:14:54.603 --> 00:14:56.938
I'm gonna go and get some
clean towels for him.

254
00:15:26.635 --> 00:15:28.219
No. fuck him!

255
00:15:28.386 --> 00:15:30.305
If he don't pay us. we ain't showing up.

256
00:15:31.222 --> 00:15:33.433
<i>And he won't have any ring girls
for his next fight.</i>

257
00:15:40.023 --> 00:15:41.232
Where's Zeek?

258
00:15:41.399 --> 00:15:42.759
<i>Been asking myself the same thing.</i>

259
00:15:43.109 --> 00:15:44.837
My first day. I thought he'd
roll out the red carpet.

260
00:15:44.861 --> 00:15:46.321
Yeah. well. you know Zeek.

261
00:15:46.446 --> 00:15:48.615
His idea of a welcome
is not throwing a chair.

262
00:15:48.782 --> 00:15:50.158
Right.

263
00:15:50.325 --> 00:15:52.952
So Simeon's ghostin' us.
and now Zeek's vanished too...

264
00:15:53.745 --> 00:15:54.745
Fuck!

265
00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:57.207
Why is she so irritated?

266
00:15:57.374 --> 00:15:59.459
Well. we haven't been paid
for the last few events.

267
00:16:00.043 --> 00:16:03.213
And Jasmine's kind of like our
self-appointed union boss.

268
00:16:04.255 --> 00:16:05.590
You don't seem too fussed.

269
00:16:06.132 --> 00:16:09.177
Simeon's always late.
that's just him. but...

270
00:16:10.011 --> 00:16:12.514
it is a bit weird that he's
not picking up his phone though.

271
00:16:12.681 --> 00:16:13.890
<i>Do you know where he is?</i>

272
00:16:14.015 --> 00:16:16.351
No. I ain't seen him.

273
00:16:17.519 --> 00:16:18.519
Anyway...

274
00:16:19.187 --> 00:16:20.187
Yeah.

275
00:16:31.449 --> 00:16:32.534
So...

276
00:16:32.992 --> 00:16:34.119
first day.

277
00:16:34.244 --> 00:16:36.079
I guess I should get you a welcome gift.

278
00:16:36.538 --> 00:16:40.417
I appreciate it. but.
no gifts needed for me.

279
00:16:40.875 --> 00:16:42.043
Even if...

280
00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:43.461
I was the gift?

281
00:16:47.716 --> 00:16:52.387
Get your mind out the gutter. Kilroy.

282
00:16:52.554 --> 00:16:54.347
I'm offering my help with Kareem.

283
00:16:55.515 --> 00:16:57.308
<i>He's fighting at York Hall
tomorrow isn't he?</i>

284
00:16:58.101 --> 00:17:00.395
And what makes you so
confident I need your help?

285
00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:01.896
Well...

286
00:17:02.355 --> 00:17:04.733
You said it yourself. I know boxing.

287
00:17:06.109 --> 00:17:08.309
Yeah. you got potential.
but I'd need to see more of you

288
00:17:08.403 --> 00:17:10.488
before I decide if you're
skilled enough for that.

289
00:17:11.406 --> 00:17:13.283
So you do want to see me again?

290
00:17:16.327 --> 00:17:17.662
Zeek's at York Hall.

291
00:17:17.787 --> 00:17:19.587
We should get down there
before he pisses off.

292
00:17:20.832 --> 00:17:21.832
Yeah...

293
00:17:22.208 --> 00:17:23.752
Hopefully I'll see you at York Hall.

294
00:18:12.926 --> 00:18:14.052
Jay!

295
00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:18.389
Hey. Lorik...

296
00:18:18.556 --> 00:18:20.433
haven't seen you in ages. bruv.

297
00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:21.810
You good?

298
00:18:21.976 --> 00:18:23.287
Piece of shit. what're you doing here?

299
00:18:23.311 --> 00:18:24.604
Just come for a drink. man.

300
00:18:24.729 --> 00:18:26.332
Yeah. I like what
you've done with the place.

301
00:18:26.356 --> 00:18:27.398
All right.

302
00:18:28.691 --> 00:18:30.068
Out please. out. out. ladies. out.

303
00:18:30.235 --> 00:18:32.320
Come on. Hurry up please.

304
00:18:32.487 --> 00:18:35.031
Fam. this is the guy
I was telling you lot about.

305
00:18:35.448 --> 00:18:37.534
<i>The best debt collector in London.</i>

306
00:18:38.117 --> 00:18:39.117
Aye.

307
00:18:40.286 --> 00:18:41.406
tell them your catch phrase.

308
00:18:41.496 --> 00:18:42.705
No Lorik.

309
00:18:42.872 --> 00:18:44.266
they don't wanna
hear my catch phrase. man.

310
00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:46.376
<i>Aye. yeah. We want. we want.</i>

311
00:18:47.877 --> 00:18:48.877
Yeah...

312
00:18:49.587 --> 00:18:50.587
well...

313
00:18:51.714 --> 00:18:54.968
“If you ever need someone
to pay. just hit up Jay!”

314
00:19:01.724 --> 00:19:04.269
I told you guys this fucker is crazy.

315
00:19:04.811 --> 00:19:06.938
I'm having a post-party
at my place tonight.

316
00:19:07.730 --> 00:19:09.667
You should come around. I may
have some more work for you.

317
00:19:09.691 --> 00:19:13.027
- Yeah man. I'll be there. yeah.
- All right. I'll see you later.

318
00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:14.820
Go.

319
00:19:16.531 --> 00:19:19.325
Fuckin' crazy guy... fuck.

320
00:19:36.551 --> 00:19:37.991
And something that's always played

321
00:19:38.094 --> 00:19:41.055
a- a-a-a vital role
in our enjoyment of sport.

322
00:19:41.890 --> 00:19:42.891
is betting.

323
00:19:43.057 --> 00:19:44.475
Sports betting

324
00:19:44.642 --> 00:19:47.228
is a one hundred billion dollar
industry and growing...

325
00:19:51.524 --> 00:19:52.817
Mr. Morton.

326
00:19:53.651 --> 00:19:55.211
Could I have five minutes of your time?

327
00:19:55.361 --> 00:19:56.195
I'd love to discuss with you...

328
00:19:56.362 --> 00:19:57.780
Three hundred seconds?

329
00:19:58.197 --> 00:19:59.282
That's a luxury.

330
00:19:59.449 --> 00:20:01.034
The lift takes twenty six seconds.

331
00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:03.453
- that's how long you got.
- I'm Cebella Marshall.

332
00:20:03.620 --> 00:20:05.371
I've already tried calling you.

333
00:20:07.457 --> 00:20:10.001
Knew there was a reason
I was avoiding you.

334
00:20:10.335 --> 00:20:11.628
Your father's reputation

335
00:20:11.794 --> 00:20:14.631
doesn't exactly scream
above board. does it?

336
00:20:14.756 --> 00:20:15.965
And yours does?

337
00:20:16.966 --> 00:20:18.527
You used offshore
shell companies to outbid

338
00:20:18.551 --> 00:20:20.303
a government-backed deal in Manila.

339
00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:21.512
Made thirty million.

340
00:20:21.679 --> 00:20:23.264
No headlines. no arrests.

341
00:20:24.349 --> 00:20:25.099
That's not judgment.

342
00:20:25.266 --> 00:20:26.392
That's appreciation.

343
00:20:26.976 --> 00:20:28.311
Well. I'm not naïve.

344
00:20:28.478 --> 00:20:30.205
I just think you're the
only person sharp enough

345
00:20:30.229 --> 00:20:32.690
and bold enough to help me
make this happen.

346
00:20:34.734 --> 00:20:35.985
Make what happen?

347
00:20:36.152 --> 00:20:37.654
Vegas in London.

348
00:20:39.072 --> 00:20:42.283
We already have casinos
in London. Miss Marshall.

349
00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:43.450
True.

350
00:20:43.743 --> 00:20:45.244
But unlike in America.

351
00:20:45.411 --> 00:20:47.531
our casinos don't allow
sports betting inside of them.

352
00:20:47.622 --> 00:20:50.792
I'm sure you already know this.
but in January alone.

353
00:20:50.959 --> 00:20:52.669
the casino sports books in Nevada made

354
00:20:52.835 --> 00:20:56.798
seventy-two point six million
dollars in gross gaming revenue.

355
00:20:57.298 --> 00:21:01.177
I want to bring sports books
to casinos in London.

356
00:21:01.844 --> 00:21:04.389
Specifically. my casino.

357
00:21:07.141 --> 00:21:08.893
Well. that's been tried before.

358
00:21:09.394 --> 00:21:10.770
Never got government support.

359
00:21:10.937 --> 00:21:12.105
A lot of vested interest.

360
00:21:12.689 --> 00:21:17.193
Yes. but... if someone were to be
the first to crack the code.

361
00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:19.028
they stand to make...

362
00:21:19.487 --> 00:21:22.448
billions in an untapped market.

363
00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:27.161
Are you interested?

364
00:21:28.371 --> 00:21:29.872
Well. that depends.

365
00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:33.126
It won't be straightforward.

366
00:21:34.043 --> 00:21:36.337
Are you willing to do what it takes?

367
00:21:36.504 --> 00:21:37.588
I'm willing...

368
00:21:38.089 --> 00:21:40.633
to do whatever it takes
to make this happen.

369
00:21:47.598 --> 00:21:48.933
I'll be in touch.

370
00:21:55.606 --> 00:21:57.442
I'm not getting anything from this.

371
00:21:58.026 --> 00:21:59.527
It's just employment records.

372
00:22:00.069 --> 00:22:01.463
He's got a few gaps here and there.

373
00:22:01.487 --> 00:22:03.573
Two year one. a three year one. but...

374
00:22:03.740 --> 00:22:04.991
Let me see it.

375
00:22:15.001 --> 00:22:16.001
<i>These gaps...</i>

376
00:22:16.044 --> 00:22:17.545
<i>someone like Simeon?</i>

377
00:22:18.546 --> 00:22:19.881
They're arrests.

378
00:22:21.090 --> 00:22:23.342
And all of a sudden.
he's wearing a recording device?

379
00:22:23.509 --> 00:22:25.094
Nah.

380
00:22:25.219 --> 00:22:27.430
This ain't just some cop operation.

381
00:22:28.556 --> 00:22:30.433
He's working with the feds.

382
00:22:31.517 --> 00:22:32.560
Fuck.

383
00:22:33.144 --> 00:22:34.312
That means the NCA.

384
00:22:36.189 --> 00:22:38.441
Amado's not gonna be happy
with cops sniffing around.

385
00:22:38.608 --> 00:22:39.877
We need to find Simeon's handler

386
00:22:39.901 --> 00:22:41.319
<i>and find out what they know.</i>

387
00:22:41.652 --> 00:22:44.238
Look. Look. they're comin' out.

388
00:22:51.162 --> 00:22:53.039
<i>Security closing the door...</i>

389
00:22:55.416 --> 00:22:56.834
Should be empty now.

390
00:22:57.293 --> 00:22:58.293
Let's go.

391
00:23:32.286 --> 00:23:33.996
All right. dump the stash there.

392
00:23:40.002 --> 00:23:41.002
Jay...

393
00:23:41.921 --> 00:23:43.214
There's someone here.

394
00:23:49.887 --> 00:23:51.013
Go!

395
00:23:57.019 --> 00:23:58.688
- Where'd he go?
- How should I know.

396
00:23:59.105 --> 00:24:00.690
Where the fuck is he?

397
00:24:02.150 --> 00:24:04.318
- Check the rest of the club.
- Yeah.

398
00:24:17.790 --> 00:24:19.000
Come on. you motherfucker!

399
00:24:19.125 --> 00:24:21.502
Let's play. you and me!

400
00:24:47.862 --> 00:24:49.906
Fuck. This is bad.

401
00:24:50.364 --> 00:24:51.532
That's Nadim's son.

402
00:24:51.949 --> 00:24:55.620
Hate to admit it. but your amigo's right.

403
00:24:58.664 --> 00:25:00.041
No. not necessarily.

404
00:25:00.917 --> 00:25:02.060
All right. here's what we do.

405
00:25:02.084 --> 00:25:03.628
Go get the drugs from the office.

406
00:25:14.597 --> 00:25:15.806
Duke. what are you thinkin'?

407
00:25:16.724 --> 00:25:18.924
We'll leave one of the duffels
behind and burn the rest.

408
00:25:18.976 --> 00:25:20.394
And when Nadim finds his son.

409
00:25:20.561 --> 00:25:22.289
stabbed the fuck up with
Marshall drugs all around him.

410
00:25:22.313 --> 00:25:23.481
he'll call Zeek and Cebella

411
00:25:23.648 --> 00:25:25.168
demanding answers
that they won't have.

412
00:25:25.233 --> 00:25:26.567
And they'll want to know how

413
00:25:26.734 --> 00:25:28.337
their drugs got there in the first place.

414
00:25:28.361 --> 00:25:30.088
And we're gonna make 'em
think it's the Russians.

415
00:25:30.112 --> 00:25:32.198
- Think it'll work?
- I do.

416
00:25:32.782 --> 00:25:34.617
We just need Lorik here to do his part.

417
00:25:34.742 --> 00:25:37.078
Let's give him a proper Russian send-off.

418
00:25:38.663 --> 00:25:39.997
Give me the knife.

419
00:25:52.301 --> 00:25:55.513
<i>Listen. Duke's a
legend. he'd be a massive draw.</i>

420
00:25:56.264 --> 00:25:58.144
<i>Our streaming partners
are over the moon on this</i>

421
00:25:58.307 --> 00:26:00.577
<i>and I'm willing to do a seventy
thirty split on the purse.</i>

422
00:26:00.601 --> 00:26:02.401
Like I told the others
that called before you.

423
00:26:02.478 --> 00:26:03.646
I'm not Duke's manager.

424
00:26:04.063 --> 00:26:05.481
<i>But you are his father.</i>

425
00:26:05.982 --> 00:26:08.651
<i>and if anyone can help him see
how good an opportunity this is.</i>

426
00:26:08.818 --> 00:26:10.236
<i>it's you.</i>

427
00:26:10.403 --> 00:26:12.464
<i>I blast this bitch out
to my twenty million followers.</i>

428
00:26:12.488 --> 00:26:14.240
<i>I bet we could get him fifteen million.</i>

429
00:26:14.407 --> 00:26:15.241
What. quid?

430
00:26:15.408 --> 00:26:17.076
<i>No cap.</i>

431
00:26:17.201 --> 00:26:19.361
<i>People are clamoring to see
The Duke in the ring again.</i>

432
00:26:19.662 --> 00:26:20.847
<i>I just want to give them what they want.</i>

433
00:26:20.871 --> 00:26:22.248
<i>you know what I'm sayin'?</i>

434
00:26:23.416 --> 00:26:24.917
So. you doing deals for me now?

435
00:26:25.084 --> 00:26:26.210
I ain't making shit for you.

436
00:26:26.335 --> 00:26:27.878
The phone rang. I answered it.

437
00:26:28.671 --> 00:26:29.831
Didn't sound like that to me.

438
00:26:29.922 --> 00:26:31.465
I don't care how it sounds to you.

439
00:26:32.008 --> 00:26:33.648
but these people are looking to slide you

440
00:26:33.718 --> 00:26:34.927
fifteen million quid

441
00:26:35.052 --> 00:26:37.013
to knock out some American reality star.

442
00:26:37.179 --> 00:26:39.265
And what if that's not what I want to do?

443
00:26:40.725 --> 00:26:44.186
Y'know. I don't know what
the hell you wanna do Duke.

444
00:26:44.353 --> 00:26:45.396
and I don't care.

445
00:26:45.980 --> 00:26:48.024
But what I do know.
is from where I'm standin'.

446
00:26:48.774 --> 00:26:50.585
you ain't got nothin'.
And that phone's been ringin'

447
00:26:50.609 --> 00:26:52.689
off the hook with offers
to get you back in the ring.

448
00:26:52.820 --> 00:26:53.980
Least you could do is listen.

449
00:26:54.071 --> 00:26:55.698
I don't give a shit about boxing.

450
00:26:56.365 --> 00:26:57.765
I got bigger things to worry about.

451
00:26:57.825 --> 00:26:58.825
Bigger things.

452
00:26:58.951 --> 00:27:00.411
What bigger things?

453
00:27:07.460 --> 00:27:08.460
Look.

454
00:27:09.587 --> 00:27:11.672
if you don't want to box again.
that's your choice.

455
00:27:13.049 --> 00:27:15.426
But you need to find something
that makes you happy.

456
00:27:56.675 --> 00:27:57.675
Langston?

457
00:27:57.927 --> 00:27:59.387
Yes. Mrs. Marshall?

458
00:28:02.223 --> 00:28:04.266
You drove my husband before. correct?

459
00:28:05.017 --> 00:28:07.144
On and off for the past three years.

460
00:28:07.311 --> 00:28:08.311
How was he?

461
00:28:08.896 --> 00:28:10.564
Aye. he always treated me fairly.

462
00:28:10.731 --> 00:28:12.358
No complaints from my end.

463
00:28:15.027 --> 00:28:16.737
Before Kingsley left. did he...

464
00:28:17.113 --> 00:28:18.739
mention where he was going?

465
00:28:20.366 --> 00:28:21.534
Not at all.

466
00:28:24.203 --> 00:28:26.483
I'll be posted outside if you
need further transportation.

467
00:28:30.584 --> 00:28:32.128
Langston?

468
00:28:32.962 --> 00:28:34.922
I. won't be needing any

469
00:28:35.214 --> 00:28:36.799
transportation today.

470
00:28:37.758 --> 00:28:39.385
The rest of the day is yours.

471
00:28:41.971 --> 00:28:43.931
I'm sorry. Mrs. Marshall. but I've been...

472
00:28:44.515 --> 00:28:46.559
instructed not to let you out of my sight.

473
00:28:47.476 --> 00:28:49.311
Langston. when I say you're done...

474
00:28:49.979 --> 00:28:50.979
you're done.

475
00:28:51.480 --> 00:28:52.480
K?

476
00:28:55.234 --> 00:28:56.485
As you wish.

477
00:28:57.987 --> 00:28:59.280
I'll see you in the morning.

478
00:29:21.510 --> 00:29:22.510
Wow.

479
00:29:23.804 --> 00:29:25.222
Hey...

480
00:29:30.394 --> 00:29:31.979
You hire the place out?

481
00:29:32.146 --> 00:29:33.146
Mmhmm.

482
00:29:33.522 --> 00:29:34.648
Nah. nah. nah.

483
00:29:34.815 --> 00:29:36.150
All the kids are at school.

484
00:29:36.317 --> 00:29:37.485
Does anyone bunk anymore?

485
00:29:38.194 --> 00:29:40.279
Maybe this generation
ain't bad breed like us.

486
00:29:40.446 --> 00:29:41.780
True.

487
00:29:44.283 --> 00:29:45.951
Your brother practically lived here.

488
00:29:49.246 --> 00:29:51.183
Remember when they used to make
you wear the bowling shoes?

489
00:29:51.207 --> 00:29:52.291
Yeah. yeah. yeah.

490
00:29:52.458 --> 00:29:54.335
Calvin would not have it.

491
00:29:54.793 --> 00:29:56.837
Nah. he used to say that people
and their feet

492
00:29:56.962 --> 00:29:58.005
couldn't be trusted here.

493
00:29:58.172 --> 00:29:59.590
Mmhmm.

494
00:29:59.882 --> 00:30:01.217
Listen. he was right.

495
00:30:01.383 --> 00:30:02.383
Man...

496
00:30:05.971 --> 00:30:07.515
Listen...

497
00:30:08.474 --> 00:30:10.809
about the other night. at the gym.

498
00:30:10.935 --> 00:30:12.311
It wasn't what it looked like.

499
00:30:12.478 --> 00:30:13.788
it was just an innocent
conversation. that's all.

500
00:30:13.812 --> 00:30:15.314
Why you think I care. Duke?

501
00:30:15.981 --> 00:30:18.359
You're free to do whatever you want.

502
00:30:24.031 --> 00:30:25.199
How's your dad?

503
00:30:26.700 --> 00:30:27.910
Still miserable.

504
00:30:28.327 --> 00:30:29.703
I don't know. we've just...

505
00:30:30.329 --> 00:30:31.705
picked up where we left off.

506
00:30:31.872 --> 00:30:33.752
You two are as bad as each
other. you know that.

507
00:30:33.999 --> 00:30:35.143
You always took his side. man.

508
00:30:35.167 --> 00:30:36.835
Well he was always nice to me.

509
00:30:37.836 --> 00:30:38.879
So. what're you sayin'?

510
00:30:39.463 --> 00:30:41.090
You gonna play somethin'?

511
00:30:41.215 --> 00:30:42.383
Come...

512
00:30:42.550 --> 00:30:43.717
let me smash you up.

513
00:30:44.635 --> 00:30:46.637
Listen. we're not in the ring. you know.

514
00:30:47.179 --> 00:30:49.431
We're not in the ring.
we're eye to eye. we're equals.

515
00:30:49.598 --> 00:30:51.141
Stop talkin'. Just pick a game.

516
00:30:51.308 --> 00:30:52.768
That's all you got to do.

517
00:30:54.562 --> 00:30:56.647
You really want that smoke?

518
00:30:57.314 --> 00:30:58.583
They couldn't get me off the table

519
00:30:58.607 --> 00:31:00.047
when we used to go Knights remember?

520
00:31:00.109 --> 00:31:02.653
Knights Youth Club.

521
00:31:03.153 --> 00:31:05.114
I used to love that place. man.

522
00:31:05.239 --> 00:31:06.239
<i>Wow.</i>

523
00:31:08.200 --> 00:31:10.119
Okay. here we go.

524
00:31:13.872 --> 00:31:16.000
Has Kingsley got a table
at home or somethin'?

525
00:31:25.509 --> 00:31:27.761
You ever think for a moment that...

526
00:31:29.263 --> 00:31:32.433
maybe Kingsley had something
to do with Calvin in Vegas?

527
00:31:35.185 --> 00:31:36.437
Where's that come from?

528
00:31:37.313 --> 00:31:38.314
Just...

529
00:31:39.148 --> 00:31:41.150
Here we are. repeating ourselves.

530
00:31:42.610 --> 00:31:44.111
What if he found out about us then?

531
00:31:44.278 --> 00:31:46.158
I wouldn't put anything
past that man if he did.

532
00:31:46.238 --> 00:31:48.157
He didn't.

533
00:31:49.950 --> 00:31:51.368
If he did...

534
00:31:53.162 --> 00:31:54.455
I would be gone...

535
00:31:56.707 --> 00:31:58.584
And my brother would still be here.

536
00:32:03.964 --> 00:32:06.425
What are you gonna do
with your life now. Duke?

537
00:32:07.009 --> 00:32:08.677
The ring was always your home.

538
00:32:09.678 --> 00:32:11.430
At least. you were happiest there.

539
00:32:14.141 --> 00:32:15.392
I don't know.

540
00:32:17.770 --> 00:32:19.146
But this is a start.

541
00:32:21.148 --> 00:32:22.941
Being here. me and you...

542
00:32:27.029 --> 00:32:28.614
What are we doing. Duke?

543
00:32:29.657 --> 00:32:30.866
Really?

544
00:32:36.622 --> 00:32:38.207
Making up for lost time.

545
00:32:40.918 --> 00:32:42.544
No. no.

546
00:32:45.172 --> 00:32:46.215
You're an asshole.

547
00:32:46.965 --> 00:32:48.050
You're an asshole.

548
00:32:48.425 --> 00:32:50.010
You come back after all this time

549
00:32:50.135 --> 00:32:52.429
kicking off feelings I haven't
thought about in years!

550
00:32:52.971 --> 00:32:54.848
Do you know how unfair that is to me?

551
00:32:59.311 --> 00:33:01.355
You think any of this was fair for me?

552
00:33:07.903 --> 00:33:11.073
I had everything I wanted
eight years ago.

553
00:33:12.991 --> 00:33:14.326
And in one moment...

554
00:33:16.161 --> 00:33:17.663
it was all taken away.

555
00:33:19.873 --> 00:33:22.000
But I never stopped loving you.

556
00:33:22.167 --> 00:33:23.919
I stopped. Duke.

557
00:33:26.046 --> 00:33:27.297
I had to.

558
00:33:28.340 --> 00:33:29.883
Because if I didn't...

559
00:33:32.261 --> 00:33:34.388
I couldn't have kept on breathing.

560
00:33:45.607 --> 00:33:47.067
Then why did you come here?

561
00:33:59.455 --> 00:34:01.957
I gotta go.

562
00:34:02.082 --> 00:34:03.167
Hey...

563
00:34:04.752 --> 00:34:06.170
Please...

564
00:34:08.714 --> 00:34:10.466
We can't keep playing games. Duke.

565
00:34:26.607 --> 00:34:27.941
So let me get this straight.

566
00:34:28.692 --> 00:34:31.487
Our load. or part of it
was found with Nadim and them.

567
00:34:31.653 --> 00:34:32.696
Not Nadim...

568
00:34:33.280 --> 00:34:34.114
Lorik.

569
00:34:34.281 --> 00:34:35.574
But Nadim wants to meet.

570
00:34:36.617 --> 00:34:37.701
Bullshit.

571
00:34:37.868 --> 00:34:39.411
He said it was something important.

572
00:34:39.578 --> 00:34:40.889
I don't give two shits what
he wants to talk about!

573
00:34:40.913 --> 00:34:42.581
Shhh... for fuck's sake.

574
00:34:44.041 --> 00:34:47.211
If it's a sprinkle that
was found. then it's a ton.

575
00:34:48.128 --> 00:34:49.296
<i>This all bullshit. you know?</i>

576
00:34:49.463 --> 00:34:50.798
They're tryin' us.

577
00:34:51.173 --> 00:34:53.091
Dad's not around. so they hit us.

578
00:34:53.425 --> 00:34:54.218
Ain't no respect!

579
00:34:54.384 --> 00:34:55.719
Respect is earned.

580
00:34:55.886 --> 00:34:57.763
Nadim's gotta be spanked.

581
00:34:58.889 --> 00:34:59.889
Yeah...

582
00:35:00.224 --> 00:35:01.809
Nadim's gotta be spanked.

583
00:35:01.975 --> 00:35:03.018
Lorik too.

584
00:35:03.185 --> 00:35:04.412
That's what dad would do
if he was here...

585
00:35:04.436 --> 00:35:06.021
- But he isn't here.
- So?

586
00:35:06.188 --> 00:35:08.774
He taught us both
so we should lean on that.

587
00:35:10.359 --> 00:35:12.653
He would make an example
out of him and you know it.

588
00:35:13.487 --> 00:35:15.697
So what you want to do then bro?

589
00:35:31.004 --> 00:35:32.004
Kill him.

590
00:35:33.924 --> 00:35:35.259
We can't do that.

591
00:35:35.717 --> 00:35:36.844
Why not?

592
00:35:40.097 --> 00:35:41.348
All right.

593
00:35:42.307 --> 00:35:44.351
All right. you tell me the next step.

594
00:35:45.310 --> 00:35:46.621
We send a couple of heads 'round there

595
00:35:46.645 --> 00:35:47.688
to scope out the place.

596
00:35:47.855 --> 00:35:49.022
before we go down.

597
00:35:50.399 --> 00:35:52.568
If it looks sideways.

598
00:35:53.026 --> 00:35:54.361
we make it straight.

599
00:36:01.201 --> 00:36:02.870
Beauty for mine eyes.

600
00:36:03.036 --> 00:36:05.372
Hi Zeek.

601
00:36:05.497 --> 00:36:06.874
- Cebella...
- Joy.

602
00:36:09.501 --> 00:36:11.211
I'm gonna let you two be.

603
00:36:13.255 --> 00:36:15.048
I'll see you later Cece.

604
00:36:27.019 --> 00:36:28.645
You needed something Cebella?

605
00:36:29.313 --> 00:36:30.355
Sounded important.

606
00:36:30.522 --> 00:36:32.107
You almost got someone fired today.

607
00:36:32.232 --> 00:36:33.232
Who?

608
00:36:33.275 --> 00:36:34.275
Langston?

609
00:36:35.319 --> 00:36:36.695
Let me guess.

610
00:36:36.820 --> 00:36:38.506
you didn't like the fact
that I gave him the day off.

611
00:36:38.530 --> 00:36:40.699
I didn't like the fact
he didn't follow instructions.

612
00:36:40.824 --> 00:36:43.577
Cebella. this cannot be a continual thing.

613
00:36:44.828 --> 00:36:46.188
I'm fine with him being my driver.

614
00:36:46.330 --> 00:36:48.057
- but when I say go. he goes.
- No. you don't.

615
00:36:48.081 --> 00:36:50.792
And why the hell do I need
anyone keeping tabs on me?

616
00:36:50.918 --> 00:36:52.669
No one's keeping tabs on you.

617
00:36:53.045 --> 00:36:55.047
Just trying to keep you protected.

618
00:37:02.888 --> 00:37:04.765
What is this really about Cebella?

619
00:37:05.807 --> 00:37:07.351
Why do you hate me so much?

620
00:37:07.935 --> 00:37:11.146
<i>I get having a stepmom
your same age is not easy...</i>

621
00:37:11.271 --> 00:37:13.607
But at some point.
you have to get over it.

622
00:37:13.774 --> 00:37:16.443
Do you really think that's why I hate you?

623
00:37:18.612 --> 00:37:21.198
Then you are dumber than
I give you credit for.

624
00:37:29.998 --> 00:37:31.792
I'm about business...

625
00:37:32.459 --> 00:37:33.459
my own.

626
00:37:35.128 --> 00:37:38.632
You. though. is what we
like to call a leech.

627
00:37:39.216 --> 00:37:41.176
Someone that latches onto something

628
00:37:41.343 --> 00:37:43.053
and sucks it 'till it's dry.

629
00:37:43.220 --> 00:37:45.597
Just like others who have
gotten around my father.

630
00:37:46.556 --> 00:37:48.517
Luckily for him.
he's able to see through them.

631
00:37:48.684 --> 00:37:51.687
but for some reason. not you.

632
00:37:52.396 --> 00:37:54.106
Good ole Joy.

633
00:37:54.982 --> 00:37:56.066
But you don't fool me.

634
00:37:56.608 --> 00:37:58.068
Never have. never will.

635
00:37:58.694 --> 00:38:01.154
The only person you're fooling
is yourself.

636
00:38:01.905 --> 00:38:04.408
because your value isn't within yourself.

637
00:38:04.574 --> 00:38:06.910
it's who you lie on your back for.

638
00:38:23.343 --> 00:38:24.386
You know.

639
00:38:25.137 --> 00:38:27.431
<i>the difference between
a mother and child Cebella.</i>

640
00:38:29.391 --> 00:38:31.059
is that sometimes...

641
00:38:32.561 --> 00:38:34.855
you need to let a child
have a temper tantrum.

642
00:38:35.981 --> 00:38:37.941
Get some things out their system.

643
00:38:39.693 --> 00:38:41.820
Hope you feel better Cece.

644
00:38:44.072 --> 00:38:46.491
Where is Kingsley. Cebella?

645
00:38:46.658 --> 00:38:47.658
Dad...

646
00:38:48.118 --> 00:38:49.453
is where he is.

647
00:38:50.287 --> 00:38:52.080
And Langston stays with you.

648
00:38:52.581 --> 00:38:53.749
That's final.

649
00:38:56.251 --> 00:38:58.170
You don't want me to tell Kingsley?

650
00:39:02.007 --> 00:39:03.007
We clear?

651
00:39:05.218 --> 00:39:06.219
Crystal.

652
00:39:34.247 --> 00:39:35.582
Finn. finish him off!

653
00:39:35.749 --> 00:39:36.750
Come on Kareem!

654
00:39:36.917 --> 00:39:38.960
Keep your work rate up Kareem!

655
00:39:43.924 --> 00:39:45.175
Word on the street is

656
00:39:45.342 --> 00:39:47.427
they got some money
laid out on their guy.

657
00:39:47.803 --> 00:39:49.304
<i>I suggest you keep an eye on them.</i>

658
00:39:49.471 --> 00:39:51.431
By the time their boy gets knocked out.

659
00:39:51.598 --> 00:39:52.849
they'll be too drunk to care.

660
00:39:52.974 --> 00:39:54.434
I ain't worried about them.

661
00:39:55.143 --> 00:39:56.353
Confident fuck.

662
00:39:58.313 --> 00:39:59.940
When we gonna start talkin' business?

663
00:40:00.357 --> 00:40:02.400
I've got more fights lined up. Good ones.

664
00:40:03.026 --> 00:40:04.569
And I want your platform to show them.

665
00:40:04.736 --> 00:40:06.988
You think you're the only
one with fights lined up?

666
00:40:07.447 --> 00:40:09.366
Clearly not. but ain't like me.

667
00:40:10.700 --> 00:40:12.327
You not seein' this shit?!

668
00:40:13.245 --> 00:40:14.621
I got York Hall on lock.

669
00:40:14.788 --> 00:40:16.790
The ticket sales are going crazy.

670
00:40:21.753 --> 00:40:23.964
And when my man wins.
what are you gonna say?

671
00:40:24.506 --> 00:40:26.174
He's gotta win first. right?

672
00:40:26.633 --> 00:40:27.759
That's very true.

673
00:40:32.222 --> 00:40:33.807
<i>Get back-get back to the corner!</i>

674
00:40:33.932 --> 00:40:36.893
<i>Stay or I don't start counting.
Get to your corner!</i>

675
00:40:38.645 --> 00:40:39.645
Back!

676
00:40:43.483 --> 00:40:44.484
One!

677
00:40:44.985 --> 00:40:45.986
Two!

678
00:40:48.446 --> 00:40:49.489
Three!

679
00:40:49.948 --> 00:40:51.283
Get back to the corner now!

680
00:40:51.449 --> 00:40:52.659
Get back!

681
00:40:52.784 --> 00:40:54.703
<i>- Slow count. slow count!</i>
- Fuckin' time!

682
00:40:54.870 --> 00:40:55.954
<i>Four!</i>

683
00:40:56.329 --> 00:40:57.330
<i>Five!</i>

684
00:40:58.206 --> 00:40:59.291
<i>Six!</i>

685
00:41:00.167 --> 00:41:01.209
<i>Seven!</i>

686
00:41:01.751 --> 00:41:02.751
<i>Eight!</i>

687
00:41:03.628 --> 00:41:05.308
How you feeling?
Are you feeling all right?

688
00:41:05.797 --> 00:41:07.048
Keep your hands up. yeah?

689
00:41:07.215 --> 00:41:08.215
Okay. breathe.

690
00:41:08.300 --> 00:41:09.426
Let's go. Fight!

691
00:41:13.930 --> 00:41:15.515
<i>All right. Kareem. you're in.</i>

692
00:41:15.640 --> 00:41:18.435
<i>- Sit down. sit down. sit down.
- Arms out. arms out.</i>

693
00:41:18.602 --> 00:41:20.896
Hey. let me talk to him.
Let me talk to him!

694
00:41:22.105 --> 00:41:24.191
Oi. listen. hit him low. twice.

695
00:41:24.357 --> 00:41:25.609
- What?
- Right. trust me.

696
00:41:25.775 --> 00:41:27.152
Why would I do that?

697
00:41:27.319 --> 00:41:28.111
Right. look. I know this
guy's type. all right?

698
00:41:28.278 --> 00:41:29.404
He's a hothead.

699
00:41:29.571 --> 00:41:31.531
Hit him low. he'll do something stupid.

700
00:41:32.157 --> 00:41:33.992
and he'll get disqualified.

701
00:41:35.327 --> 00:41:36.536
All right? You want to win?

702
00:41:36.703 --> 00:41:37.703
Do it. Go.

703
00:41:45.420 --> 00:41:47.172
Low blow! Fuck's sake Ref!

704
00:41:48.298 --> 00:41:50.717
Keep 'em up! Above the belt line!

705
00:41:50.842 --> 00:41:52.219
Fight! Keep going.

706
00:41:58.725 --> 00:42:01.478
No. that's fine. that's above
the waistline. keep boxing!

707
00:42:04.231 --> 00:42:07.234
Ay! Ref! What the fuck was that?

708
00:42:07.525 --> 00:42:08.777
Cheating bastard!

709
00:42:08.902 --> 00:42:10.070
<i>Ref. what the fuck was that?!</i>

710
00:42:10.195 --> 00:42:11.235
<i>He fuckin' headbutted him!</i>

711
00:42:11.363 --> 00:42:13.156
Disqualify him! DQ him!

712
00:42:13.323 --> 00:42:16.076
That's-that's it! Fight's over!
Fight's over! That's it!

713
00:42:35.929 --> 00:42:38.431
Well. you hit the nail on the
head creating a spectacle.

714
00:42:38.598 --> 00:42:40.141
Boxing loves that.

715
00:42:41.351 --> 00:42:42.351
So?

716
00:42:42.936 --> 00:42:43.936
We'll talk.

717
00:43:11.006 --> 00:43:13.174
DU-KE!

718
00:43:13.341 --> 00:43:14.175
<i>Whoo!</i>

719
00:43:14.342 --> 00:43:15.343
<i>Big W's!</i>

720
00:43:15.719 --> 00:43:17.846
That's what I'm talkin' about. boy!

721
00:43:20.724 --> 00:43:22.809
Fuck you say to Kareem?

722
00:43:22.976 --> 00:43:25.854
Spit bucket guys don't normally
give advice like that in corner.

723
00:43:26.229 --> 00:43:27.480
Kareem...

724
00:43:27.647 --> 00:43:29.899
He ain't ready for
a guy like that. Not now.

725
00:43:30.066 --> 00:43:31.377
It could have gone
a hundred more rounds

726
00:43:31.401 --> 00:43:32.652
and he wasn't gonna win.

727
00:43:32.819 --> 00:43:34.779
Only way he was is if
the ref called a DQ.

728
00:43:35.864 --> 00:43:37.449
So I told him how to get one.

729
00:43:38.950 --> 00:43:41.244
Zeek. man. I saw what was going on.

730
00:43:42.704 --> 00:43:43.830
What you talkin' about?

731
00:43:44.289 --> 00:43:47.292
The ref. the count. how you looked.

732
00:43:48.335 --> 00:43:50.587
I ain't green to this mate.
the fix was clearly in.

733
00:43:51.254 --> 00:43:52.589
but it wasn't working.

734
00:43:53.214 --> 00:43:55.614
And your dad had a reputation
for doing this back in the day.

735
00:43:55.925 --> 00:43:57.361
But no one could ever pin
anything on him

736
00:43:57.385 --> 00:43:58.720
because he was precise.

737
00:43:59.387 --> 00:44:02.265
So if you're going to do it.
you need the right people.

738
00:44:03.058 --> 00:44:04.351
to make it happen...

739
00:44:06.895 --> 00:44:07.895
And I can help you.

740
00:44:08.104 --> 00:44:09.344
I didn't know you were a cheat.

741
00:44:09.647 --> 00:44:10.690
What's changed?

742
00:44:12.650 --> 00:44:13.943
Eight years...

743
00:44:15.987 --> 00:44:17.030
it changes a lot.

744
00:44:22.535 --> 00:44:24.415
Look. I don't know what
I got to do to prove it.

745
00:44:26.456 --> 00:44:27.707
If you need me.

746
00:44:28.625 --> 00:44:29.625
I'm here for you.

747
00:44:35.924 --> 00:44:37.092
<i>Zeek Marshall!</i>

748
00:44:38.176 --> 00:44:40.136
Your fighter's a cheatin' bastard.

749
00:44:40.804 --> 00:44:42.055
Here we fuckin' go.

750
00:44:42.430 --> 00:44:43.765
Gents. the fight's over.

751
00:44:43.932 --> 00:44:45.392
Time to make your way to the exit.

752
00:44:45.558 --> 00:44:48.978
No one's fuckin' leavin'
till we get justice for our boy.

753
00:44:49.521 --> 00:44:51.481
- Now. we want a rematch.
- Yeah?

754
00:44:52.440 --> 00:44:54.543
Last time I checked. headbutts
weren't allowed in the ring.

755
00:44:54.567 --> 00:44:57.695
Well your guy started fightin' dirty first.

756
00:44:57.821 --> 00:44:59.406
and now we've lost a lot of money.

757
00:44:59.572 --> 00:45:03.118
Lads. lads. la-it's-look.
it's been a long night.

758
00:45:03.284 --> 00:45:04.786
let's just take this up another time.

759
00:45:04.911 --> 00:45:07.664
No one's fuckin' talkin' to you. murderer.

760
00:45:08.373 --> 00:45:10.166
<i>Hey. get the fuck out of here</i>

761
00:45:10.333 --> 00:45:12.252
before you talk yourself into trouble.

762
00:45:13.837 --> 00:45:16.089
Now. if you want me
to throw you out myself...

763
00:45:17.424 --> 00:45:18.466
<i>I can.</i>

764
00:45:18.925 --> 00:45:21.052
Really?

765
00:45:28.143 --> 00:45:29.727
It's all right. It's all right.

766
00:45:30.937 --> 00:45:33.064
Now get the fuck out
before it gets worse.

767
00:45:33.731 --> 00:45:35.859
Little Zeek brought his killer along.

768
00:45:37.277 --> 00:45:38.570
Pick him up. Tommy.

769
00:45:39.571 --> 00:45:40.738
<i>This ain't over Zeek.</i>

770
00:45:40.905 --> 00:45:43.074
You're just another fuckin' toe rag

771
00:45:43.241 --> 00:45:44.701
tryin' to be king of the hill.

772
00:45:44.868 --> 00:45:45.994
Yeah? Fuck off.

773
00:45:46.161 --> 00:45:48.037
Be seein' you around big boy!

774
00:45:48.788 --> 00:45:49.873
Vonda.

775
00:45:51.374 --> 00:45:53.668
You good?

776
00:45:54.294 --> 00:45:56.671
Yeah.

777
00:45:57.422 --> 00:45:58.756
You saved my ass there.

778
00:45:59.340 --> 00:46:00.508
I owe you one.

779
00:46:00.925 --> 00:46:02.177
You're family.

780
00:46:02.343 --> 00:46:04.103
I'd never let anyone
do anything to you Zeek.

781
00:46:04.220 --> 00:46:05.220
Ever.

782
00:46:10.768 --> 00:46:12.604
I'll buck you at the
gym in the morning. yeah?

783
00:46:13.021 --> 00:46:14.021
Yeah...

784
00:46:20.069 --> 00:46:21.529
Yo. hold up a sec.

785
00:46:24.949 --> 00:46:26.910
I need you to come somewhere with me.

786
00:46:27.702 --> 00:46:28.828
Now.

787
00:46:30.872 --> 00:46:32.308
I'm supposed to be meeting someone...

788
00:46:32.332 --> 00:46:33.332
Duke.

789
00:46:34.000 --> 00:46:35.376
I need some extra backup.

790
00:46:39.797 --> 00:46:40.797
Let's roll.

791
00:47:08.451 --> 00:47:10.495
What the fuck is Duke doin' here?

792
00:47:10.662 --> 00:47:12.205
We'll talk about it later.

793
00:47:19.337 --> 00:47:21.422
You got some explaining to do. Nadim.

794
00:47:22.215 --> 00:47:23.883
Speech of the year if you ask me.

795
00:47:24.717 --> 00:47:26.844
- Why was our pack at your spot?
- Pack...

796
00:47:27.887 --> 00:47:28.638
that's all you're worried about?

797
00:47:28.805 --> 00:47:29.889
Cut the bullshit. Nadim.

798
00:47:30.056 --> 00:47:31.336
- Where's our load?
- You load...

799
00:47:31.432 --> 00:47:33.226
isn't the point of discussion.

800
00:47:54.122 --> 00:47:56.541
<i>I'm sure you both recognize him.</i>

801
00:47:58.209 --> 00:48:00.044
<i>My beautiful son.</i>

802
00:48:00.461 --> 00:48:01.588
Dead!

803
00:48:03.131 --> 00:48:05.258
Right next to your pack!

804
00:48:05.758 --> 00:48:08.595
Looks to me that Lorik
took it upon himself

805
00:48:08.761 --> 00:48:11.306
to rob from us
and got caught by someone.

806
00:48:11.973 --> 00:48:13.933
You tried to make a move.
and it backfired.

807
00:48:14.100 --> 00:48:17.145
Why the fuck would I make a move
and kill my son in the process?

808
00:48:17.270 --> 00:48:19.731
That's for you to know innit?
Either way. give us our shit.

809
00:48:19.897 --> 00:48:21.274
Fuck you!

810
00:48:21.441 --> 00:48:23.601
You want to lose someone
you love to know how it feels?

811
00:48:24.110 --> 00:48:25.445
You threatening me?

812
00:48:26.529 --> 00:48:28.364
I could snap my fingers right now

813
00:48:28.489 --> 00:48:29.699
and all of you would be dead.

814
00:48:29.824 --> 00:48:30.824
Right...

815
00:48:31.159 --> 00:48:32.535
Z...

816
00:48:32.702 --> 00:48:34.702
Nadim. explain to me what's
goin' on from your end.

817
00:48:36.039 --> 00:48:37.457
Fucking Russians.

818
00:48:37.624 --> 00:48:38.958
Son of a bitch Nikolai!

819
00:48:39.125 --> 00:48:41.002
<i>He had it out for us since the beginning.</i>

820
00:48:41.419 --> 00:48:43.004
He did all this.

821
00:48:43.546 --> 00:48:46.090
- I can't just go off a hunch.
- A hunch?!

822
00:48:47.634 --> 00:48:51.679
The Russians cut out the tongue
of those they don't trust!

823
00:48:53.014 --> 00:48:55.600
They always want to send a message.

824
00:48:57.226 --> 00:48:59.729
I'll do my best to find out who did this...

825
00:49:00.688 --> 00:49:03.128
But I can't have you going to
war with the Russians right now.

826
00:49:03.191 --> 00:49:04.442
<i>It's not good for anyone!</i>

827
00:49:05.026 --> 00:49:06.110
<i>We need calm...</i>

828
00:49:06.486 --> 00:49:08.988
and for everyone to get back to work!

829
00:49:10.990 --> 00:49:12.116
I promise.

830
00:49:12.492 --> 00:49:13.492
I'll figure it out.

831
00:49:16.204 --> 00:49:17.580
My son dies.

832
00:49:17.747 --> 00:49:19.499
one of theirs does as well.

833
00:49:20.166 --> 00:49:22.877
<i>Your father. would have no hesitation.</i>

834
00:49:24.420 --> 00:49:25.672
It's either blood...

835
00:49:26.339 --> 00:49:27.339
or war.

836
00:49:28.305 --> 00:50:28.756
Do you want subtitles for any video?
